  "behavior": {
    "unstage": "Compare immutable base/previous/current Git blobs using minimal line edit distance. Pure partial unstage adds no new Stage request; mixed new input still does. Earlier unsubmitted Stage authorization is retained for its remaining staged content; obsolete queued/running receipts are cancelled without an unstage-only replacement.",
    "bounds": "Text comparison is bounded to 2 MiB per blob and a 20-second observation budget with 10-second Git command timeouts. Unavailable objects/binary content/limits yield an unavailable observation, not a guessed unstage.",
    "legacyWatch": "Hash-only observations establish blob history once, retaining already pending paths without guessing the missing delta.",
    "manualPriority": "Encrypted CAS orders manual interest against automatic model admission in the same profile/repository/worktree. The service also checks before executor preparation; already admitted reviews continue. Heartbeat renews 30-second manual priority while waiting or running.",
    "expiredPriority": "Expiry releases scheduling priority only. Existing unknown model execution is still interrupted on lease inspection and is never implicitly retried.",
    "waitingReason": "Service receipts and extension status distinguish manual-priority from review-budget. A retry timestamp that expires during caller cleanup keeps the payload queued."
  },
